{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>יעשה זאת [shall do this].</b> The commandment that He stated, namely, to keep the Sabbath from profaning it. It is known that שבת has the sign of a vav for feminine. Perhaps this comes as if he said 'the day of Sabbath,' or the vav of מחללו may be understood as the profaning of it being kept, for with every [active] participle the noun is in the force of language [i.e., grammatically implied] even if not written, as R. Moses the Cohen, of blessed memory, explained regarding the word ותצפנה (Joshua 2:4), that it refers back to 'the spies,' and similarly וברב יועצים תקום (Proverbs 15:22), the meaning being 'counsel,' even though not written:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 56, :notes {0 "Resolved רבי משה הכהן to 'R. Moses the Cohen' without further identification; the construction 'בכח הלשון' is rendered hyper-literally as 'in the force of language,' as the passage is grammatically dense and resists smoother phrasing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:50.995908256Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}